From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:09:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll-unix: port env, process, loader, server and thread
 replacements onto wine-11.18 thread data

wine-11.18 moved the per-thread server fds, tid and suspend flag into
struct thread_data (thread_data_key), allocates the first TEB in
init_startup_info and keeps the main image in main_module. loader: start the
main thread in 11.18's order, probe the x18 TSD slot before the TEB exists and
publish the first TEB once it does; a pseudo-process child gets its own
thread data and saves/restores main_module around its boot. env: init_peb
keeps the child's own module. server: requests use data->request_fd and
reply_fd, and server_init_thread does the iOS parts of the removed
start_thread (QoS hook, TEB publication). thread: create_server_thread and
pthread_exit_wrapper take the thread data.

Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-wine-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
